 ## Not checked
-- Windows restart on a fixed port: `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` plus TIME_WAIT (about 2 minutes) may make a restart bind fail, and the conflicting bind may raise `PermissionError` (WSAEACCES) instead of `EADDRINUSE`. The tests avoid it by using port 0 (the system picks a free port).
-- The hashes in `requirements-dev.txt` are for all files PyPI listed when it was made; `requirements-dev.txt` verified by a successful `pip install --require-hashes` in a clean `python:3.12-slim` container (Linux x86_64, Python 3.12.16, SQLite 3.46.1). `requirements-dev-win.txt` verified by `pip install --require-hashes` into a throwaway venv on the Windows laptop (Python 3.13.3). Not tested: other Linux architectures, the GitHub CI runner image.
+- Windows restart on a fixed port: `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` plus TIME_WAIT (the short wait after a connection closes; its length was not measured here) may make a restart bind fail, and the conflicting bind may raise `PermissionError` (WSAEACCES) instead of `EADDRINUSE`. The tests avoid it by using port 0 (the system picks a free port).
+- The lock files were made with the hash option (`--generate-hashes` in the headers), which by the tools' documentation lists the files PyPI offered for each pinned version when the file was made; that was not re-checked here (no network). The author reports a successful `pip install --require-hashes` of `requirements-dev.txt` in a clean `python:3.12-slim` container (Linux x86_64, Python 3.12.16, SQLite 3.46.1) and of `requirements-dev-win.txt` into a throwaway venv on the Windows laptop (Python 3.13.3); these are the author's own runs, no log is shipped, and they were not repeated here. Not tested: other Linux architectures, the GitHub CI runner image.
 - bandit B101 on tests: tests are excluded from bandit, so not relevant.
 - gitleaks is a separate program (version and checksum pinned in `.github/workflows/lint.yml`), not part of the lock files. pre-commit and exiftool are not used.
